cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Canopy height for the Essential Biodiversity Variable Ecosystem Vertical Profile from ESA BIOMASS and NASA GEDI: Beni lowland forests, Bolivia, on WGS84 HEALPix"
abstract: >-
  A dataset for the GEO BON Essential Biodiversity Variable Ecosystem Vertical
  Profile (class Ecosystem Structure) for the forest focus group of the Beni
  savanna-forest mosaic, Bolivia: ecosystem height from ESA BIOMASS Level-2A
  forest height (2026), ecosystem cover, structural complexity and the relative
  vertical profile from NASA GEDI L2A/L2B version 3, and forest from ESA
  WorldCover 2021, all on HEALPix depth 11 on the WGS84 ellipsoid. Each variable
  carries its definition quoted from its product documentation. Compared on 1,900
  forest cells, BIOMASS forest height is lower than GEDI canopy height on average
  (mean -3.0 m, 95 percent block-bootstrap interval -4.4 to -1.1 m; lower in 78
  percent of cells) but not in low canopies, and ranks forests only moderately
  consistently (Spearman 0.58). Outcome: partially supported. Includes a
  Snakemake pipeline, jupytext notebooks, the per-cell store and a FORRT
  nanopublication chain.
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
